            <div xml:id="d690">

                <pb facs="0826" n="730" sameAs="frus:frus1921v02/pg730"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861a.01/65: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at
                        Vladivostok</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Macgowan</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-09-01T18:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">September 1,
                                1921—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your 95, August 27, 1 p.m.</p>
                <p>1. Does deposed Vladivostok government now functioning in Maritime Province
                    cooperate with Moscow? 2. Does its territory include Kamchatka, Anadir and
                    mainland Sakhalin? 3. Is its territorial control effective? 4. In what respect
                    does it differ from Chita? 5. What are its relations with present Vladivostok
                    government? 6. With Japan? 7. Has it separate government organization, army and
                    capital?</p>
                <p>Cable reply to above and mail despatch covering detailed history of Siberian
                    governments supplementing your despatch 85, of January 15, 1921.<anchor n="39"
                        xml:id="d690-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
